# a-crew-that-was-told — plan 29 O4, and it is the OTHER HALF.
#
# ⚠⚠ **`a-crew-out-of-earshot.keys` and `a-crew-that-was-told.keys` are
# the same file except for TWO LINES: `remit 0 build` and
# `remit 1 build`.**  Same ground, same core, same spawn, same wave
# list, same crew, same drive, same ticks spent — so the difference in
# the clock is the ORDER and can be nothing else.
#
# ⚠ The crew stand FIVE hexes from the line the player draws, which is
# outside an untrained crew member's own senses (3 hexes,
# `skill.loft::DETECT_BASE_HEXES`) — so the semi-automatic default finds
# nothing and the sibling's wall is never raised.
#
# ⚠⚠ **A REMIT REACHES THE WHOLE MAP** (`@X297`): a crew member told
# *build* hunts build orders wherever they are, so these two walk the
# five hexes and raise the wall the other file's crew never notice.
# **That is what a trip out to somebody buys**, and it is the price of
# the narrowing — from now on they will do nothing else.
#
# ── What the player does ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Parks at (5, -2), presses paint, and drives to (5, 2) — which orders
# FIVE hexes: the one it was standing on when the mode came on, plus the
# four it enters.  That is the band's whole walkable height, so the wall
# would SEAL if anybody raised it.
#
# ⚠⚠ **The recon window is what pays for it** (`@X022`): the wave list
# does not start until the player pokes a spawn marker, so the ticks
# spent building are free — which is the design claim this pair makes
# measurable for the first time.

echo told to build: the same wall, and two crew who were given an order

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 12 -2
drag -3 -1 12 -1
drag -3 0 12 0
drag -3 1 12 1
drag -3 2 12 2
count painted 80 80

# ⚠⚠ The crew, standing FIVE HEXES from the line the player is about to
# draw — one clear of an untrained crew member's own senses.  Nobody has
# told them anything, so nobody comes.
crew 0 -1
crew 0 1

# ⚠⚠ **THE TWO LINES THIS PAIR TURNS ON.**  In the game they are one
# press of **G** each, standing beside the person — `@X156` makes
# presence the interaction, so the whole cost is the drive out.
remit 0 build
remit 1 build

# ── The build (or not) ──────────────────────────────────────────
park 5 -2
paint on
drive 5 2
tick 6
count orders 5 5
paint off

# Park clear of the line so the trail is not rubbed out, and let the
# crew work.  60 helper-seconds over two helpers is 30 s = 45 ticks,
# plus the walk out to it — which nobody ordered.
drive 0 0
tick 50
# ⚠ Nothing left ordered: they walked five hexes and raised it.
count orders 0 0
count painted 80 80
# ⚠⚠ The whole band, hex by hex — because a wall with ONE gap in it
# buys nothing at all (`plans/12` § B7 measured a gate at +1 tick), so
# *five* is the number that matters rather than *some*.
kind 5 -2 wall
kind 5 -1 wall
kind 5 0 wall
kind 5 1 wall
kind 5 2 wall


# ── The waves — identical to `an-undefended-base` ───────────────
wave 5
count alive 5 5

tick 22
wave 8
count alive 13 13

# ── The clock ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ **A TRIP OUT TO SOMEBODY IS WORTH +34 TICKS — 140 against 174**
# (`@M070`), two lines apart.  The `out-of-earshot` half has the same
# ground, the same core, the same spawn, the same wave list, the same
# crew in the same hexes and the same drive; what it does not have is
# somebody having been told.
#
# ⚠⚠ **And 174 is the ceiling `@M050` and `@M069` both land on** — the
# wall gets raised, so the base plays exactly as it does when the crew
# were parked on the line or standing two hexes off it.  What the order
# buys is not a better wall: it is REACH, and reach is only worth
# anything when the work is out of earshot.
#
# ⚠ The price is on the other side of the ledger and no scenario here
# measures it: from now on these two will do nothing but build
# (`@X297`), so the heap by the core is somebody else's problem.
fall 900
ticks 172 176
count idle 0 2
snap o4_a_crew_that_was_told
